<title>FRANCE: Bull, Motorola in new PowerPc pact.</title>
<headline>Bull, Motorola in new PowerPc pact.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French computer maker Groupe Bull and Motorola of the U.S. said on Thursday they had agreed a new strategic deal concerning the indirect sale of computer systems based on the PowerPC processor.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal Motorola will be responsible for the indirect sales of such systems of either maker in the U.S. and Canada while Bull will be responsible for these sales in Europe, South America and Africa.</p>
<p>Bull and Motorola have been working together on the PowerPC chip since 1994.</p>
</text>
